    <string name="opt_pin_body">Paste a link to a show from any app. It appears on the shelf, and OK on it opens that show.</string>
    <string name="opt_pin_off">Turn on Top Shelf (in Apple TV style) to pin shows from your phone.</string>
    <string name="opt_pin_offline">The TV is not on a network, so your phone cannot reach it.</string>
    <string name="desc_style">Apple TV style puts one row of apps in a glass dock over your wallpaper; Down slides the rest up. Classic shows the clock and every row at once.</string>
    <string name="desc_layout">Rows scroll sideways. Grid wraps every app onto lines you can see at once.</string>
    <string name="desc_columns">How many apps fit across the dock.</string>
    <string name="desc_tiles">The size of every app tile.</string>
    <string name="desc_peek">A sliver of the next row under the dock, so you can see there is more below.</string>
    <string name="desc_position">Bottom moves the rows to the lower edge and leaves the middle of the screen to the wallpaper.</string>
    <string name="desc_labels">When an app\'s name shows under its tile.</string>
    <string name="desc_background">Your wallpapers rotate through the photos in the wallpapers folder. Adaptive and Aurora follow the colour of the focused app.</string>
    <string name="desc_rotate">How often the home screen moves to the next photo.</string>
    <string name="desc_dim">Darkens the photo so tiles and text stay readable.</string>
    <string name="desc_accent">The focus ring and highlights across the home screen.</string>
    <string name="desc_tile_style">Afterglow puts the app\'s icon in the corner over a soft wash of its colour.</string>
    <string name="desc_icon_pack">Use an installed icon pack for app tiles. Hold OK on a tile to pick one app\'s icon.</string>
    <string name="desc_chips">Icons keep the corner quiet; a button\'s name appears when it has the focus.</string>
    <string name="desc_order">Recently used moves the app you last opened to the front.</string>
    <string name="desc_all_apps">A second section with every installed app under your pinned ones.</string>
    <string name="desc_inputs">HDMI, antenna and AV inputs as tiles on the home screen.</string>
    <string name="desc_switch">Which app switches the TV to an input when you pick it.</string>
    <string name="desc_shelf">Continue Watching from the focused app above the dock, plus the shows you pin.</string>
    <string name="desc_library">A banner of the titles you hand-picked. Hidden anyway while it is empty.</string>
    <string name="desc_clock">How the time is written in Classic style.</string>
    <string name="desc_memory">Free memory under the date, for TVs that run short. It shows only; it frees nothing.</string>
    <string name="desc_lock">Hides Options, Settings and the tile menu. Hold Menu on the home screen to unlock.</string>
    <string name="desc_next_wallpaper">Skip to the next photo now. Play/Pause on the home screen does the same.</string>
    <string name="desc_apps_on_home">Pick which apps are on the home screen.</string>
    <string name="desc_inputs_on_home">Pick which inputs show on the home screen.</string>
    <string name="desc_export">Write a copy of your settings to the TV\'s media folder, to adb pull or move to another TV.</string>
    <string name="desc_reset">Put the apps back in their default order and names. Your other choices stay.</string>
    <string name="desc_amazon">Show Amazon\'s own home screen once. Home on the remote brings dumbtv back.</string>
    <string name="recorder_label">dumbtv home Top Shelf (what apps play)</string>
    <string name="opt_tmdb_credit">Pictures for titles whose app sends none come from TMDB. This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.</string>
